  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A butter dish cover is a small domed cotton disc worked from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "magic ring",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": a flat top in double crochet spirals outward, then the sides work straight to create a short skirt that drops over the rim of a butter dish. Sized for a standard 15 cm round butter dish. Keeps the butter covered on the table and reduces plastic wrap use. One 50 m ball of DK cotton makes two covers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
